session:pr669Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #513 (split from the #373 owl2rdf umbrella) asked for the RDF encoding of the n-ary (n>2) forms of DisjointClasses/DisjointObjectProperties/DisjointDataProperties/DifferentIndividuals -- owl2rl2datalog::owl_to_rdf's binary (n=2) forms of all four already translated to a single pairwise triple, with the n>2 fallthrough hitting a generic skip. Checked provenance for owl_to_rdf.rs/owl2rl2datalog first (PRs #650, #654, #370, #433): confirmed the module's established pattern of a shared helper reused across call sites (mirroring #512's data_range generalization and #510's rdf_list reuse from the DisjointUnionOf PR), and that the binary cases were untouched precedent to build alongside. Wrote a single shared Translator::all_disjoint helper (mint blank node, type it as owl:AllDisjointClasses/owl:AllDisjointProperties/owl:AllDifferent, attach owl:members over an rdf:List) and wired it into the four n>2 match arms. The advisor caught a real correctness bug before it shipped: my first draft reified annotations via the module's usual owl:Axiom pattern (used by SubClassOf, property chains, HasKey, ...), but fetching the actual W3C mapping spec text (section 2.3.3, 'Axioms Represented by Blank Nodes') showed this axiom family is an explicit exception -- since the base translation already mints its own blank node _:x, annotations attach directly to _:x as plain triples, not via a second reification blank node. Rewrote all_disjoint and the two annotation tests to match the spec text, added an axiom_reification_count(&ds) == 0 assertion to prove no owl:Axiom node gets minted for this family. Adding n>2 arms to class_axiom/object_property_axiom/data_property_axiom made every variant of ClassAxiom, ObjectPropertyAxiom and DataPropertyAxiom covered explicitly, so the trailing 'other => self.skip(...)' catch-all in each of those three match statements became a rustc/clippy-flagged unreachable pattern and was removed -- an exhaustiveness improvement caught only because clippy -D warnings ran, not planned upfront. Cross-checking the write side against rdf_owl_translator's read-back arms (per the #179/#433 round-trip fidelity pipeline) surfaced two genuine read-back gaps this PR deliberately does not fix (out of owl_to_rdf's own scope): owl:AllDifferent is never matched in extract_axiom at all (filed as #667), and the owl:AllDisjointProperties read-back arm always reconstructs DisjointObjectProperties even when the members are data properties (filed as #668). Separately, main at e22f8e7 had an unrelated pre-existing compile break in dagalog-kernel (#662, already independently found and fixed by another agent in PR #663); rather than wait, cherry-picked #663's one-line fix commit onto this branch to unblock the workspace-wide clippy/CI gate, documented as a to-be-dropped commit once #663 merges and this branch rebases." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:669 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr669 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr669Decision .

session:pr669Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Attach n>2 DisjointClasses/DisjointObjectProperties/DisjointDataProperties/DifferentIndividuals annotations directly to the axiom's own blank node (_:x <ap> T(av)), per the mapping spec's section 2.3.3 carve-out for axiom forms that already mint their own blank node." ;
    agp:alternative "Reify via the module's usual owl:Axiom blank node (as done for SubClassOf, property chains, HasKey, DisjointUnion's owl:disjointUnionOf triple), matching every other annotated axiom in this module. Initially implemented this way and it passed self-written tests, but it is not what the W3C spec actually specifies for this exact axiom family -- rejected after fetching and quoting the spec text directly rather than trusting the module's other local conventions." .
